cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "FrontierForge: a Trainium run simulator and exact-oracle score prediction"
abstract: >-
  ffsim predicts the steps, step time and validation bits-per-byte of a
  language-model training recipe on AWS Trainium without spending chip time.
  It combines a numpy surrogate fitted on 1,206 Trainium run records with a
  GPU proxy that replays the Trainium schedule step for step. The release also
  documents the exact-oracle method (a deterministic cold chip rehearsal plus a
  near-constant offset predicts the official score), the best Phase 1 recipe
  from the AWS Trainium Frontier challenge, and the findings behind it.
